commit efea3093454ff4e467af5fbae0d602a7837ee74f

C03: the explicit folder clarification must ask which folder (FILES1439)

FILES1437 measured the current-directory count: the Spanish forms asked which folder, but the English variant («How many files are in the current directory?») produced «How many files are in the folder?», a restatement that never asks for the folder, because the explicit clarification contract only requires a question mark and the missing field name.

llm.formulate_explicit_clarification_question: for the folder field of filesystem.known.search the question must ask which folder (cuál/qué/which/what next to carpeta/directorio/folder/directory), with one corrected retry that names the known folders; otherwise the turn does not publish that question. Mind only. Tests not run (owner order).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>


